{"timestamp": "2026-09-23T13:48:29.981923", "data": {"url": "https://www.datarefs.com/top-reports/most-visited-websites-in-the-world/", "title": "100 Most Visited Websites in the World 2026 (Global Rankings)", "content": "Skip to content 100 Most Visited Websites in the World 2026 (Global Rankings) Written By Akashdeep Singh Last Updated on August 27, 2026 Download Summary Sources & Methodology Data as of August 2026 2,206 visits per second 190.6M daily active users TABLE OF Content Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the World 2026 The Rise of AI: ChatGPT Enters the Top 5 Top 100 Most Visited Websites in the World (11-100) Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the US Conclusion: Google is the Most Visited Website in the World Share Post : Copy LinkedIn X Facebook Google gets more than 100 billion visits, making it the most visited website in the world by a huge margin. But the sites behind it reveal where internet attention is shifting. YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, and Reddit still command huge audiences, while ChatGPT has entered the top five. Shopping, social media, video, and AI now shape the web\u2019s biggest traffic numbers. In this article, we\u2019ll cover the top-visited websites in the world in 2026, the US, and the rise of AI. Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the World 2026 These are the top 10 websites getting the most visits worldwide, from Google and YouTube to social media, AI, and messaging platforms. No. Website Visits Category Visit Duration 1 google.com 105.85 billion Search 21m 45s 2 youtube.com 57.05 billion Video/Social Media 37m 13s 3 facebook.com 10.32 billion Social Media 24m 34s 4 instagram.com 6.70 billion Social Media 19m 14s 5 chatgpt.com 6.12 billion AI 17m 26s 6 reddit.com 5.46 billion Social/Forums 18m 46s 7 wikipedia.org 4.40 billion Reference 15m 03s 8 x.com 4.25 billion Social Media 22m 58s 9 pornhub.com 3.84 billion Adult 16m 19s 10 whatsapp.com 3.12 billion Messaging 33m 48s Let\u2019s look at the top 10 most visited websites in detail. 1. Google.com \u2014 105.85 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 5.67 Bounce Rate 37.05% Visit Duration 21m 45s Desktop share 30.22% Mobile share 69.78% Google is the front door to the internet for most people. It handles nearly 90% of searches worldwide and billions of searches every day. Most people come here, find what they need, and leave quickly. Google is more than just a search engine. It brings together Search, Gmail, Maps, Images, News, and Chrome under one roof. That\u2019s a big reason its traffic is far ahead of every other website. Google handles more than 5 trillion searches a year. Its AI answers now appear at the top of search results, helping people find information without leaving the page. Source: Google 2. YouTube.com \u2014 57.05 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 8.95 Bounce Rate 28.91% Visit Duration 37m 13s Desktop share 33.20% Mobile share 66.80% YouTube keeps people on the site longer than any other website in the top 10, with merely 37 minutes per visit. One video leads to another, then another. For many people, it has become a mix of a search engine, classroom, and TV. YouTube is owned by Google and is the second-largest search engine in the world after Google. People use it every day to watch tutorials, listen to music, news, gaming videos, and kids\u2019 shows. It is also one of the first sites many people open after Google. Source: Texas A&M 3. Facebook.com \u2014 10.32 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 9.49 Bounce Rate 43.54% Visit Duration 24m 34s Desktop share 51.98% Mobile share 48.02% Facebook is still the biggest social network by web visits, even as younger users move to other apps. It has a near even split between desktop and mobile traffic, which is unusual for a site this large. Facebook has around 3.07 billion monthly active users, giving it a much bigger audience than its website traffic alone. Groups, Marketplace, video, and the main feed keep people coming back. Its audience also tends to be older and broader than some of its newer rivals. Source: Statista 4. Instagram.com \u2014 6.70 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 10.03 Bounce Rate 47.16% Visit Duration 19m 14s Desktop share 46.61% Mobile share 53.39% Instagram gets more pages per visit than any other site in the top 10, with more than 10 pages per session. People move quickly between Reels, stories, posts, and profiles, often without stopping for long. Instagram is Meta\u2019s photo and video platform. Reels compete directly with TikTok, while the platform has also become a popular place to search for food, travel, fashion, and shopping ideas. The website numbers don\u2019t show its full reach because most people use Instagram through the mobile app. 5. ChatGPT.com \u2014 6.12 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 4.05 Bounce Rate 37.48% Visit Duration 17m 26s Desktop share 78.12% Mobile share 21.88% ChatGPT is the first AI tool/platform to break into the global top five most visited sites, and it did so in under three years since its launch. People use it for writing, coding, research, studying, and everyday questions. Some tasks that once started with a Google search now start with ChatGPT instead. Its traffic is so heavily focused on desktop, with about 78% of visits coming from desktop. That suggests many people use it as a work and study tool rather than mainly for casual browsing. 6. Reddit.com \u2014 5.46 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 3.72 Bounce Rate 56.2% Visit Duration 18m 46s Desktop share 39.05% Mobile share 60.95% Reddit is where people go for answers from other people. Many users now add \u201creddit\u201d to a Google search when they want real opinions, personal experiences, or advice. Its communities cover almost every topic, from fixing things at home to niche hobbies and everyday problems. Google and AI tools also use information from Reddit threads, which brings even more people to the site. However, it has a high bounce rate, which makes sense. Many visitors arrive from search, read a post or two, and leave once they find what they need. 7. Wikipedia.org \u2014 4.40 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 3.49 Bounce Rate 57.66% Visit Duration 15m 03s Desktop share 26.90% Mobile share 73.10% Wikipedia is proof that a free website with no ads can still rank among the busiest sites in the world. Many people use it as a first stop for facts and background information. Wikipedia is run by a nonprofit and relies on donations and volunteers. Its information is also used across Google, voice assistants, and many AI tools. Most of its visitors use phones, with nearly three-quarters of traffic coming from mobile devices. Its place on the list shows how much people still rely on a free source of information. 8. X.com \u2014 4.25 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 9.78 Bounce Rate 43.11% Visit Duration 22m 58s Desktop share 44.49% Mobile share 55.51% X, formerly Twitter, is still one of the first places people go to see what is happening right now. News, sports, politics, and live reactions move quickly across the platform. People often jump from one post to a thread, then to another post or profile. That explains its high number of pages per visit. The switch from Twitter to X also split some traffic between x.com and the old twitter.com address. That is why twitter.com appears lower down the top 100 list. 9. Pornhub.com \u2014 3.84 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 7.42 Bounce Rate 23.97% Visit Duration 16m 19s Desktop share 10.15% Mobile share 89.85% Adult websites make up a significant share of global traffic, and Pornhub is the biggest. It ranks ninth in this list, with nearly 90% of its visits coming from mobile devices. It also has the lowest bounce rate in the top 10. Most visitors view more than one page before leaving. It\u2019s included because the list is based on actual web traffic. Leaving out a major site simply because of its content would give a less accurate picture of how people use the internet. 10. WhatsApp.com \u2014 3.12 billion visits Metric Value Pages/Visit 4.58 Bounce Rate 61.87% Visit Duration 33m 48s Desktop share 86.85% Mobile share 13.15% WhatsApp closes out the top 10, but its website traffic doesn\u2019t come close to showing its true reach. More than 3 billion people use WhatsApp to message and call. Most people use the mobile app, while the website is mainly used for WhatsApp Web, downloads, and account access. In many parts of the world, WhatsApp is one of the main ways people stay in touch every day. That\u2019s why its web traffic only tells part of the story. Source: Statista The Rise of AI: ChatGPT Enters the Top 5 For the first time, an AI tool has entered the top five most visited websites in the world. The speed of that rise is what stands out. ChatGPT launched in November 2022 and reached the global top five in about three years. Its weekly user base also grew from around 400 million to 900 million in a year, showing just how quickly people have adapted to using AI tools. ChatGPT isn\u2019t the only AI site growing. Several others have climbed into the top 100. Website Rank Monthly visits chatgpt.com 5 6.12 billion claude.ai 30 1.10 billion openai.com 49 542.69 million deepseek.com 71 332.96 million grok.com 97 216.90 million The bigger story is how people find information. The questions that once started with Google now start with an AI chatbot. People use these tools to write, research, code, study, and get quick answers without opening several websites. AI is also changing Google itself. Its AI Overviews can answer many questions directly on the search results page, reducing the need to click through to another site. The rise of ChatGPT is more than a new name in the top 10. It\u2019s a sign that the way people search, learn, and find information is changing. Top 100 Most Visited Websites in the World (11-100) Below the top 10 is a mix of shopping, streaming, social media, adult, news, and other popular websites. These sites may not match the traffic of the biggest names above, but many still attract millions of visits every month. Here is the list of the top 100 most visited websites in the world. No. Website Visits Category 11 tiktok.com 2.68 billion Social Media/Video 12 amazon.com 2.42 billion Shopping 13 yahoo.com 2.41 billion Search/Portal 14 xvideos.com 2.40 billion Adult 15 duckduckgo.com 2.14 billion Search 16 bing.com 1.98 billion Search 17 yahoo.co.jp 1.86 billion Search/Portal 18 weather.com 1.73 billion Weather 19 linkedin.com 1.68 billion Social / Professional 20 xhamster.com 1.66 billion Adult 21 msn.com 1.56 billion Portal/News 22 netflix.com 1.46 billion Streaming 23 pinterest.com 1.31 billion Social Media/Discovery 24 twitch.tv 1.29 billion Video/Streaming 25 temu.com 1.25 billion Shopping 26 microsoft.com 1.23 billion Technology 27 live.com 1.23 billion Email/Productivity 28 gihub.com 1.14 billion Technology/Developer 29 yandex.ru 1.13 billion Search 30 claude.ai 1.10 billion AI 31 xnxx.com 1.09 billion Adult 32 discord.com 1.08 billion Messaging/Social 33 spotify.com 920.06 million Music 34 naver.com 881.15 million Search/Portal 35 imdb.com 847.34 million Entertainment/Reference 36 canva.com 794.19 million Design 37 roblox.com 788.04 million Gaming 38 apple.com 757.74 million Technology 39 paypal.com 734.57 million Finance 40 globo.com 714.01 million News/Media 41 aliexpress.com 699.81 million Shopping 42 comix.to 650.85 million Comics/Manga 43 dailymotion.com 594.92 million Video 44 twitter.com 574.53 million Social Media 45 booking.com 570.69 million Travel 46 walmart.com 562.88 million Shopping 47 ebay.com 556.74 million Shopping 48 telegram.org 548.61 million Messaging 49 openai.com 542.69 million AI 50 nytimes.com 493.01 million News 51 office.com 474.08 million Productivity 52 espn.com 453.04 million Sports 53 usps.com 448.0 million Postal/Logistics 54 amazon.de 435.13 million Shopping 55 indeed.com 433.93 million Jobs / Recruitment 56 amazon.co.jp 432.23 million Shopping 57 zoom.us 414.58 million Video Conferencing 58 vk.com 410.80 million Social 59 uol.com.br 408.80 million News/Portal 60 samsung.com 407.20 million Technology 61 adobe.com 405.70 million Technology/Software 62 onlyfans.com 405.22 million Adult 63 bbc.com 404.21 million News 64 shopify.com 392.31 million E-commerce 65 etsy.com 372.66 million Shopping 66 bbc.co.uk 360.29 million News 67 ecosia.org 358.65 million Search 68 rakuten.co.jp 347.66 million Shopping 69 accuweather.com 344.30 million Weather 70 primevideo.com 339.98 million Streaming 71 deepseek.com 332.96 million AI 72 threads.com 331.67 million Social Media 73 disneyplus.com 326.30 million Streaming 74 shein.com 321.71 million Shopping 75 quora.com 317.92 million Q&A/Reference 76 mail.ru 304.23 million Email/Portal 77 amazon.in 299.59 million Shopping 78 cnn.com 297.67 million News 79 scribd.com 288.74 million Publishing/Documents 80 marca.com 286.80 million Sports 81 amazon.co.uk 276.46 million Shopping 82 zillow.com 266.81 million Real Estate 83 opera.com 265.85 million Technology/Browser 84 note.com 257.73 million Publishing/Blogging 85 fifa.com 250.80 million Sports 86 vk.ru 247.78 million Social 87 hbomax.com 238.11 million Streaming 88 theporndude.com 236.85 million Adult 89 ozon.ru 230.94 million Shopping 90 patreon.com 227.51 million Content 91 yandex.com 226.16 million Search 92 archive.org 223.14 million Reference/Library 93 mercadolivre.com.br 221.18 million Shopping 94 theguardian.com 219.95 million News 95 ikea.com 218.41 million Shopping/Furniture 96 snapchat.com 217.13 million Social Media 97 grok.com 216.90 million AI 98 google.com.br 215.83 million Search 99 homedepot.com 215.12 million Shopping 100 atlassian.net 211.19 million Technology/Software Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the US The US list looks a little different from the global ranking. Google and YouTube still lead, but Amazon and Reddit rank higher than they do worldwide. The biggest difference is the mix of sites Americans visit most. Shopping, social media, and online communities play a bigger role, while adult sites drop out of the top 10. Here are the top 10 most visited websites in the US. No. Website Visits Category Visit Duration 1 google.com 25.31 billion Search 23m 43s 2 youtube.com 10.27 billion Video/Social Media 37m 20s 3 reddit.com 2.61 billion Social/Forums 20m 35s 4 facebook.com 2.38 billion Social Media 24m 59s 5 amazon.com 1.96 billion E-commerce 17m 02s 6 yahoo.com 1.25 billion Search/Portal 18m 10s 7 wikipedia.org 1.21 billion Reference 16m 28s 8 instagram.com 1.19 billion Social Media 18m 12s 9 chatgpt.com 1.09 billion AI 19m 35s 10 x.com 941.23 million Social Media 24m 17s Conclusion: Google is the Most Visited Website in the World The rankings may shift from month to month, but the bigger picture is clear. Google and YouTube still dominate the web, while ChatGPT has already pushed its way into the top five. However, there\u2019s an important catch. These rankings measure website visits, not app use. That means the numbers don\u2019t show the full reach of platforms like WhatsApp, Instagram, or Facebook, where much of their activity happens inside mobile apps. The top 100 still belongs largely to search, social media, video, and shopping. But the balance is starting to shift. AI is moving up the rankings fast, and its growth is changing where people go to find answers. FAQs What is the most visited website in the world? Google, with about 105.85 billion visits a month, is the most visited website in the world. No other site comes close. Is Google or YouTube more popular? Google gets more visits, but YouTube keeps people far longer, close to 37 minutes per visit. Which is the most visited AI website? ChatGPT is the most visited AI website with 6.12 billion visits, ranked fifth overall. Claude, OpenAI, DeepSeek, and Grok also appear in the top 100. Do these rankings include mobile apps? No. The rankings count website visits only. App-first platforms like WhatsApp and Facebook therefore have a much larger reach than these numbers show. Akashdeep Singh Data Analyst & Research Specialist Akashdeep has 7 years of experience in data research, validation, and analytical review. At DataRefs, he works closely with datasets and reports to ensure consistency, accuracy, and methodological clarity. His role supports the delivery of dependable, reference-grade insights used for long-term analysis and decision-making. Stay Updated Weekly Join 10,000+ professionals getting weekly insights There was an error trying to submit your form. Please try again. This field is required. Subscribe Weekly Newsletter There was an error trying to submit your form. Please try again. Must-Read Research AI SEO Statistics 2026 \u2013 Trends & Market Size Data Google\u2019s AI overviews now reach more than 2 billion people... Read More Social Media Statistics (2026) \u2013 Active Users & Demographics Social media is now available to 5.79 billion identities across... Read More Creator Economy Statistics (2026): Market Size, Earnings & Trends The creator economy is already a $216.32 billion market in... Read More Scroll to Top", "lists": [["Home", "About Us Our Team Why Trust DataRefs", "Our Team", "Why Trust DataRefs", "Statistics Artificial Intelligence SaaS Streaming Social Media", "Artificial Intelligence", "SaaS", "Streaming", "Social Media", "Market Size", "Blog"], ["Our Team", "Why Trust DataRefs"], ["Artificial Intelligence", "SaaS", "Streaming", "Social Media"], ["Home", "About Us Our Team Why Trust DataRefs", "Our Team", "Why Trust DataRefs", "Statistics Artificial Intelligence SaaS Streaming Social Media", "Artificial Intelligence", "SaaS", "Streaming", "Social Media", "Market Size", "Blog"], ["Our Team", "Why Trust DataRefs"], ["Artificial Intelligence", "SaaS", "Streaming", "Social Media"], ["Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the World 2026 The Rise of AI: ChatGPT Enters the Top 5 Top 100 Most Visited Websites in the World (11-100) Top 10 Most Visited Websites in the US Co